---
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | MD Anik Hasan"
  description="Privacy information for mdanikhasan.com, including the current no-analytics, no-form-submission state and future disclosure requirements."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Privacy record"
    title="Collect less, explain it clearly."
    intro="This site currently works without analytics, advertising trackers, accounts, cookies, or a form-submission backend."
    workshop="Privacy Record"
  />

  <article class="prose standalone">
    <h2>Current data handling</h2>
    <p>
      The public site does not currently submit, store, or process enquiry or seller-interest form
      data. It does not use analytics or advertising scripts. Search runs against a static index in
      the visitor’s browser.
    </p>

    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>
      Links to GitHub and other future verified profiles take you to another service. That service
      applies its own privacy policy and may collect information according to its settings.
    </p>

    <h2>If forms are enabled later</h2>
    <p>
      Before a contact or seller-interest endpoint is enabled, this page must identify what is
      collected, why it is needed, where it is sent, how long it is retained, and how a person can
      request deletion. Server-side validation, abuse protection, and rate limiting must be
      configured at the same time.
    </p>

    <h2>If analytics are enabled later</h2>
    <p>
      No tracking will be added silently. Any future analytics choice must be privacy-respecting,
      documented here, and configured so that no optional tracking runs before the visitor’s
      decision where consent is required.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Privacy questions can be sent to
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. The <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>
      lists the currently published communication routes.
    </p>

    <p><small>Effective date: 27 July 2026.</small></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
